 "grading": {
  "grader": "orchestrator (Claude), MY GRADE at native 1280x720; renderer three.js WebGL headless Chromium, subject nurse-rebaked-2026-09-18.glb under the Model Vetting Studio rig",
  "stills": {
   "open/closed (frames 31/41, rest blink at 1400 ms, front-facing)": "both lids close fully from the front; lips closed at rest, no teeth slab in the rest pose; the eye-crop sheet (encoded webm) shows the image-left eye (character right) keeps a blue iris sliver under a crumpled lid on all 7 close-up blinks while the image-right eye closes cleanly (unchanged from 09-17).",
   "concerned/anxious/reassured (frames 157/400/651, line midpoints)": "mouth shapes differ frame to frame (visemes now drive SS/E/U/O/aa/PP/nn); the three moods are not reliably distinguishable from the stills alone: brows are sparse specks after strand reduction and the lid/brow weights read as small offsets. Same finding as 09-17.",
   "wide (frame 907)": "full figure, textured strawberry-blond hair, teal scrubs with chest pocket, hands and forearms skin; pants read flat teal."
  },
  "questions": {
   "hairTextureVisible": "YES. Strand streaks and light/dark colour variation across the bob in every still; 09-17 hair was one flat brown factor. Hair-region luma stddev 18.1 -> 20.6 (dominated by silhouette shading; the visible change is colour/streak texture, not contrast).",
   "scrubWeaveVisible": "NO at this framing. Shirt patch (430..600,600..700) luma stddev 1.42 (09-17) -> 2.64 (09-18) on the open still; wide-shot patch 5.65 -> 4.95 (shading gradient dominates). The atlas carries the weave at 0.71-0.78x source stddev in G/B, which is ~1% of full scale at the teal mean and is below what 1280x720 resolves.",
   "scrubPocketVisible": "YES. Chest pocket seam visible bottom-right of every close-up and in the wide shot (also present on 09-17; it is geometry, not texture).",
   "skinFacets": "YES, unchanged. Large crumpled facets on cheeks, jaw, neck and forearms from the tangent-space normal bake.",
   "greyNecklinePatch": "YES, unchanged. Grey/tan T-shaped patch at the collar V below the neck in every close-up.",
   "teethSlab": "YES, unchanged. Open-mouth frames show one bright white slab, no tooth separation.",
   "moodReadable": "WEAK. Not reliably readable from a single still; brow legibility regressed vs 09-17 because the eyebrow mesh is now 1,045 tris of sparse strands (09-17 stills were rendered from an unreduced 9,597-tri brow)."
  },
  "harnessChange": "render.mjs: H.264 first attempt crf 23 -> 18 (fallback 26 -> 21). At crf 23 measure-blinks confirmed 6/7 close-up blinks in the mp4 (15367 ms open reference irisFraction 0.007 < 0.01); at crf 18 7/7. video.mp4 1.57 MB -> 2.94 MB. Frames byte-identical between the two renders (00157, 00460 sha256 equal). Edited by grok muse-spark-openrouter, 4 turns.",
  "notTested": "headset runtime; clinical readability of the moods; audio-to-mouth latency beyond Rhubarb cue timing; the 33 MB laddered GLB (3600x3600 hair albedo + normal, 10.5 MB + 10.3 MB) against any Quest budget; promotion of the rebake to the shipped path."
 }
